# Line endings, settled in the repository rather than per machine.
#
# Everything here is committed with LF, but there was no `.gitattributes`, so
# the result depended on each developer's `core.autocrlf`. On Windows with the
# default `true`, every checkout rewrote the working tree to CRLF — which is why
# `git` prints "LF will be replaced by CRLF" on almost every file it touches,
# and why a formatter configured for LF would report the entire repository as
# badly formatted after a simple `git checkout`.
#
# `eol=lf` makes the working tree match the blob on every platform, so the
# formatter, the editor and git all agree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, and must never be touched by line-ending conversion.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
